TITLE:: Pbranching
SUMMARY:: Experimental bounded tree generation
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/Pmorphism, Classes/Ppetri, Guides/Patternarium-Systems

DESCRIPTION::
Experimental: this API may change before 1.0.

Builds a single rooted tree lazily. Root metadata is depth 0 and index 0, with nil parentIndex and childIndex. Every other node contains value, depth, index, parentIndex and zero-based childIndex. Indices are assigned at child creation, so depth traversal can emit them out of numeric order.

The root is yielded before expanding it. Each resumed parent expansion receives the latest inval. Offspring is a nonnegative Integer, a per-stream Pattern sampled once for each expanded parent, or a Function(node, inval). An exhausted offspring Pattern gives zero children to subsequent parents. Parents at maxDepth are not expanded and consume no offspring values. ValueFunction(parent, childIndex, inval) computes each child's value; nil is invalid. Without it, children inherit their parent's value.

Breadth traversal uses a queue with a moving head; depth uses a stack and visits children in ascending childIndex order. MaxNodes counts the root, emitted nodes and queued nodes. The stream throws before allocating children that would exceed it. MaxNodes must be 1..1000000; maxDepth is nonnegative. The emitted node Event is a fresh shallow copy; contained values remain caller-owned, so use functional child-value updates for mutable values. Metadata copies passed to callbacks cannot change internal indices/depth.

Iteration state and offspring streams are independent. Storage is O(maxNodes), including queue references retained for breadth traversal. Finite depth with zero offspring ends in extinction. This models a tree, not a continuous-time birth/death process.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: seed
One non-nil root value, including an Array as a single value; a Function is evaluated once with inval.
ARGUMENT:: offspring
Nonnegative Integer, Pattern, or Function(node, inval).
ARGUMENT:: valueFunction
Optional Function(parent, childIndex, inval), returning a non-nil child value.
ARGUMENT:: maxDepth
Nonnegative Integer, default 8; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: maxNodes
Positive Integer, default 10000, at most 1000000; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: traversal
breadth (default) or depth; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: output
node (default) or value; sampled once. Once-sampled parameters accept literals, Functions or Patterns.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns constructor arguments in public constructor order.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Yields values and returns the latest inval when the stream ends.

EXAMPLES::
code::
Pbranching(0, 2, { |p, i| p[\value] + i + 1 }, 2, output: \value).asStream.all;
::

Tree values choose pitch/position; deeper descendants arrive faster. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pbranching / Value stream
var values = {
Pbranching(0, 2, { |p, i| p[\value] + i + 1 }, 2, output: \value).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { x[\degree] ? if(x[\value].isNumber) { x[\value] } { (x[\depth] ? 0)*3+(x[\childIndex] ? 0)*2 } } { if(x.isNumber) { x } { if(x.isArray) { x[1]*14 } { x.size*2 } } }, pan: if(x.isArray) { x[0].clip(-1,1) } { 0 }, dur: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { x[\dur] ? (0.3/((x[\depth] ? 0)+1)) } { 0.18 }, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Musical example
Load the main Guide example instruments first.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \fmPiano,
    \degree, Pbranching(0, 2, { |p, i| p[\value] + [-1, 1][i] }, 3, output: \value),
    \dur, 0.125).play;
)
::

